<title>USA: Fuel-Tech settles patent litigation.</title>
<headline>Fuel-Tech settles patent litigation.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fuel-Tech NV said on Monday it settled litigation that affirms its patent of Fuel Tech's NOxOUT process for nitrogen oxide emission control.</p>
<p>The litigation, challenging certain NOxOUT patents, was brought by ENOVA Corp's San Diego Gas &amp; Electric Co and Edison International's Southern California Edison Co, Fuel-Tech said.</p>
<p>Under terms of the settlement, the two utilities have taken a paid-up license to use the NOxOUT patent technology in their owned or controlled plants, Fuel-Tech said.</p>
<p>Also, Fuel Tech has agreed to pay the utilities a total of $275,000 as the result of the settlement of a dispute arising from a 1985 demonstration at San Diego Gas &amp; Electric's Encina plant, Fuel-Tech said.</p>
<p>The dollar amount of the paid up license was not immediately available.</p>
</text>
